' 4+1 process view - Email worker (US22) · claim with SKIP LOCKED, send, postpone, give up
' Version 1.1 - 2026-11-10
' For: whoever writes code and whoever debugs.
' Documented decision: The worker claims the messages with SKIP LOCKED, sends, postpones or gives up (ADR 0004).
' Not drawn: internal detail of the classes; refusals that do not change the sequence (they are in the text of process.md).
@startuml process-outbox
!include ../style.puml

title Process view - email worker (US22): claim with SKIP LOCKED, send, postpone, give up
autonumber

box "Outbox worker (in the API process)"
  participant "Loop" as API_NOTIF_DISPATCH
  participant "Process" as API_NOTIF_PROC
  participant "Compose" as API_NOTIF_COMPOSE
  participant "Send" as API_NOTIF_SENDER
end box
participant "Clock" as CC_TIME
database "PostgreSQL" as C_DB
participant "SMTP server" as X_SMTP <<external>>

loop until the API stops (Outbox:Enabled)
  API_NOTIF_DISPATCH -> API_NOTIF_PROC : New scope; ProcessDueAsync
  group Batch transaction
    API_NOTIF_PROC -> C_DB : SELECT * FROM outbox_messages WHERE sent_at, failed_at and\nskipped_at IS NULL AND next_attempt_at <= now ORDER BY\nnext_attempt_at, id LIMIT 20 FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED [SQL]
    note over API_NOTIF_PROC, C_DB: Another instance (or pass) skips the locked rows: they never claim the same\nmessage.\nThe locks are held while the batch is sent.
    loop each message
      API_NOTIF_PROC -> C_DB : Current recipient by the payload's id (for notices, also the\nbooking) [SELECT users]
      alt no recipient, or the message cannot be read
        API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_PROC : GiveUp(recipient_not_found or the exception type): failed_at;\nWarning with id and type
      else no longer applies
        API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_PROC : Skip(reason): skipped_at (next diagram)
      else ready
        API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_COMPOSE : Text and HTML in pt-PT, Lisbon time
        API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_SENDER : SendAsync(email)
        API_NOTIF_SENDER -> X_SMTP : One connection per message [SMTP]
        alt sent
          API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_PROC : MarkSent(now)
        else exception
          API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_PROC : RecordFailure(exception type, now, retry): attempts + 1;\nnext_attempt_at = now + 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 min (max. 1 h)
          API_NOTIF_PROC -> API_NOTIF_PROC : On the 6th failure: failed_at and Warning (id and type, never the address)
        end
      end
      API_NOTIF_PROC -> C_DB : SaveChanges of this message's result [UPDATE outbox_messages]
    end
    API_NOTIF_PROC -> C_DB : COMMIT: the results stay and the locks go [SQL]
  end
  note over API_NOTIF_PROC, X_SMTP: At least once: if the process stops after sending and before the COMMIT, the\nmessage goes out again.
  alt the batch came back full (20)
    API_NOTIF_DISPATCH -> API_NOTIF_DISPATCH : Goes straight back to the start
  else
    API_NOTIF_DISPATCH -> CC_TIME : Task.Delay(10 s, timeProvider)
  end
end
note over API_NOTIF_DISPATCH: A failure of the pass (database down)\nis logged as Error and the next pass tries again.
@enduml
